 handler then settles the job as a 504 and kills the build at once.\n\n**Scenario:** A user wants \"effectively no limit\" without knowing that `0` means that, and sets `GIT_GLOSS_ARY_TIMEOUT=3000000000`. Then every page request fails, so the server is unusable.\n\n**What I ran:** In a throwaway repo under `scratch/`:\n```\nGIT_GLOSS_ARY_TIMEOUT=3000000000 git-gloss ary --no-open\ncurl \"$url?rev=HEAD\"  →  504 in 0.12 s\nstderr: TimeoutOverflowWarning: 3000000000 does not fit into a 32-bit signed integer. Timeout duration was set to 1.\n```\n**Fix:** Clamp `timeoutMs` to 2³¹−1, or treat larger values as `0` (no limit).\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
